# Numeric Enums 🔢

Enums allow you to define a set of named constants. By default, numeric enums auto-increment starting at `0`:

```typescript
enum Direction {
  Up,    // 0
  Down,  // 1
  Left,  // 2
  Right  // 3
}

console.log("Direction Up:", Direction.Up);     // 0
console.log("Direction Left:", Direction.Left); // 2

// Custom starting value
enum HttpStatus {
  OK = 200,
  Created = 201,
  BadRequest = 400,
  NotFound = 404
}
console.log("Status OK:", HttpStatus.OK); // 200
```

