# String Enums 🔤

In string enums, each member is explicitly initialized with a string value:

```typescript
enum UserRole {
  Admin = "ADMIN",
  Editor = "EDITOR",
  Viewer = "VIEWER"
}

function checkAccess(role: UserRole) {
  if (role === UserRole.Admin) {
    console.log("Granting administrative access...");
  } else {
    console.log(`Access restricted for role: ${role}`);
  }
}

checkAccess(UserRole.Admin);
checkAccess(UserRole.Viewer);
```

