## Why String Enums are Superior:
String enums serialize clearly in logs, network payloads, and debuggers, whereas numeric enums only print opaque numbers like `0` or `1`!

# Const Enums (Zero Runtime Overhead) ⚡

Prefixing an enum with `const` completely removes the enum object from compiled JavaScript, inlining the raw literal values at compile time!

```typescript
const enum LogLevel {
  Debug = 1,
  Info = 2,
  Error = 3
}

const currentLevel = LogLevel.Info;
// Compiles directly to JavaScript: const currentLevel = 2;
console.log("Current Log Level:", currentLevel);
```

