# `Partial<T>`: Making Properties Optional ❓

`Partial<T>` returns a type with all properties of `T` set to **optional**. Essential for update/patch operations:

```typescript
interface User {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  age: number;
}

// PartialUser is { id?: number; name?: string; email?: string; age?: number }
function updateUser(id: number, fieldsToUpdate: Partial<User>): void {
  console.log(`Updating user ${id} with:`, fieldsToUpdate);
}

// Valid! Only updating email:
updateUser(101, { email: "new_email@example.com" });
```

