# `Required<T>`: Making Properties Mandatory ❗

The opposite of `Partial<T>`. `Required<T>` removes optionality, making **every single property mandatory**:

```typescript
interface AppConfig {
  title?: string;
  port?: number;
  ssl?: boolean;
}

// All properties are strictly required!
const finalConfig: Required<AppConfig> = {
  title: "Production Gateway",
  port: 443,
  ssl: true
};

console.log("Config validated:", finalConfig);
```

