# `Readonly<T>`: Immutable Data Structures 🔒

`Readonly<T>` sets all properties of `T` to `readonly`, preventing any reassignment:

```typescript
interface Task {
  title: string;
  completed: boolean;
}

const task: Readonly<Task> = {
  title: "Refactor API Controllers",
  completed: false
};

// task.completed = true; // Error: Cannot assign to 'completed' because it is a read-only property!
console.log("Readonly task:", task.title);
```

