# `Record<K, T>`: Structured Key-Value Maps 🗺️

`Record<Keys, Type>` constructs an object type whose property keys are `Keys` and values are `Type`:

```typescript
type Role = "admin" | "editor" | "guest";

interface Permissions {
  canRead: boolean;
  canWrite: boolean;
}

// Guarantees all 3 roles are defined with valid permissions!
const rolePermissions: Record<Role, Permissions> = {
  admin: { canRead: true, canWrite: true },
  editor: { canRead: true, canWrite: true },
  guest: { canRead: true, canWrite: false }
};

console.log("Guest permissions:", rolePermissions.guest);
```

