# `Pick<T, K>`: Extracting Specific Keys ✂️

Construct a new type by choosing a specific subset of keys `K` from type `T`:

```typescript
interface Article {
  id: number;
  title: string;
  body: string;
  author: string;
  views: number;
}

// Only pick 'id' and 'title' for a lightweight summary preview:
type ArticlePreview = Pick<Article, "id" | "title">;

const preview: ArticlePreview = {
  id: 42,
  title: "Mastering TypeScript Utility Types"
};

console.log("Preview:", preview);
```

