# `Omit<T, K>`: Removing Specific Keys 🗑️

The opposite of `Pick<T, K>`. Construct a type by taking all properties from `T` and **dropping keys `K`**:

```typescript
interface UserAccount {
  id: number;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  passwordHash: string; // Sensitive!
}

// Omit passwordHash for safe client-facing responses
type PublicUser = Omit<UserAccount, "passwordHash">;

const publicProfile: PublicUser = {
  id: 1,
  name: "Marcus",
  email: "marcus@example.com"
};

console.log("Public Profile:", publicProfile);
```

