# `Exclude<T, U>`: Filtering Unions 🚫

`Exclude<Union, ExcludedMembers>` removes specific member types from a union:

```typescript
type AllStatus = "idle" | "loading" | "success" | "error";

// Exclude 'error' from active running statuses
type NonErrorStatus = Exclude<AllStatus, "error">;
// Inferred as "idle" | "loading" | "success"

const currentStatus: NonErrorStatus = "loading";
console.log("Status:", currentStatus);
```

<!-- FULL_CODE_START
