# Chaining Multiple Utility Types 🔗

Utility types can be composed together for complex transformations:

```typescript
interface DatabaseUser {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  email: string;
  passwordHash: string;
  createdDate: Date;
}

// 1. Remove sensitive passwordHash
// 2. Make everything else optional for PATCH requests!
type UserPatchPayload = Partial<Omit<DatabaseUser, "passwordHash" | "id">>;

const updatePayload: UserPatchPayload = {
  email: "newemail@example.com"
};

console.log("Combined Utility Payload:", updatePayload);
```

